{"created": "2026-08-31T06:46:21.955760+00:00", "modified": "2026-09-01T07:28:03.915077+00:00", "id": 21887809, "conceptrecid": "21887808", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21887809", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.21887808", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21887809", "metadata": {"title": "ImageCAS-X", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.21887809", "publication_date": "2026-08-11", "description": "<p>ImageCAS-X is a new dataset of voxel-wise annotations of the vessel lumen and coronary segments for 800 coronary computed tomography angiography scans from the publicly available ImageCAS dataset. The dataset also includes coronary centerlines, mesh surfaces, and scan-level descriptors for coronary dominance, image quality and coronary heart disease. Pretrained weights are also included for the 6 coronary segmentation methods.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Accompanying publication: \"ImageCAS-X: a dataset and benchmark for coronary artery segmentation and centerline extraction in coronary CT angiography\" (Under review, 2026)</p>\n<p>Preprint: https://arxiv.org/abs/2608.30404</p>\n<p>Project Webpage: https://kitbransby.github.io/ImageCAS-X</p>\n<p>Code: https://github.com/kitbransby/ImageCAS-X</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Bransby, Kit Mills", "affiliation": "Technical University of Denmark", "orcid": "0009-0003-1902-6518"}, {"name": "Paulsen, Rasmus Reinhold", "affiliation": "Technical University of Denmark", "orcid": "0000-0003-0647-3215"}], "keywords": ["lumen segmentation", "coronary computed tomography angiography"], "dates": [{"type": "created"}], "language": "eng", "custom": {"code:codeRepository": "https://github.com/kitbransby/ImageCAS-X", "code:programmingLanguage": [{"id": "python", "title": {"en": "Python"}}]}, "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 0, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "21887808"}}]}}, "title": "ImageCAS-X", "links": {"self": "https: